---
// 一条事实与一个 Skill 的完整旅程：HTML 时间线，窄屏自然换行。
const { lang = 'zh' } = Astro.props;
const T = {
  zh: {
    label: { mem: '记忆', skill: 'Skill', both: '记忆 + Skill' },
    steps: [
      { when: '会话 A · 第 3 轮', lane: 'mem', title: '用户说「这个仓库以后都用 pnpm」',
        body: '前台模型调用 memory add，MEMORY.md 立刻落盘；工具返回值让模型本轮就知道写成了。记忆计数随之清零；不过本轮要不要做记忆复盘，在回合开头就已经定了，这次写入改变不了。' },
      { when: '会话 A · 第 3 轮', lane: 'mem', title: 'system prompt 里仍是旧快照',
        body: '快照在会话启动时冻结，这次写入不改它。由于这条事实就来自本会话的对话，模型的上下文里本来就有它，所以这段「过期」基本无害。' },
      { when: '会话 A · 第 9 轮', lane: 'skill', title: '一次反复试错的任务累计到 10 次模型请求',
        body: '回合末检查 Skill 计数达标，答复送出后启动 Background Review。fork 先浏览已有 Skill，确认没有可以就地修补的，再用 skill_manage 新建 pnpm-workspace-test，并标记为 created_by: agent。在支持目录变更通知的会话中，用户下一次发消息时，模型就能得知这项新 Skill。' },
      { when: '会话 A · 第 40 轮', lane: 'mem', title: '上下文压缩触发重建',
        body: 'invalidate_system_prompt() 从磁盘重读记忆，新的快照写着 pnpm。重建本来就要重新写入缓存，顺带刷新记忆几乎没有额外代价（这一句是我的推断）。' },
      { when: '会话 B · 启动', lane: 'both', title: '新会话直接看到两样东西',
        body: 'MEMORY.md 进入 system prompt；Skill 目录里出现 pnpm-workspace-test，但正文要等模型用 skill_view 打开才会读入。' },
      { when: '此后 30 天无人使用', lane: 'skill', title: 'curator 把它归档',
        body: '默认配置下，维护检查发现满 14 天无活动可标 stale，满 30 天可移入 skills/.archive/。两次检查之间跨过阈值时，也能直接归档。' },
      { when: '用户执行 restore', lane: 'skill', title: '回到 active，但时钟没有重置',
        body: '如果到下次自动转换时仍未读取、使用或修补，原活动时间仍满足归档条件，它会再次被归档。这一点我用实验确认过，见下文。' },
    ],
  },
  en: {
    label: { mem: 'memory', skill: 'skill', both: 'memory + skill' },
    steps: [
      { when: 'Session A · turn 3', lane: 'mem', title: 'The user says "always use pnpm in this repo"',
        body: 'The foreground model calls memory add and MEMORY.md is written at once; the tool result tells the model it worked. The memory counter resets, but whether this turn runs a memory review was decided when the turn began, and this write cannot change that.' },
      { when: 'Session A · turn 3', lane: 'mem', title: 'The system prompt still shows the old snapshot',
        body: 'The snapshot was frozen at session start and this write leaves it alone. The fact came from this very conversation, so the model already has it in context; the "staleness" is mostly harmless.' },
      { when: 'Session A · turn 9', lane: 'skill', title: 'A trial-and-error task reaches 10 model requests',
        body: 'At turn end the skill counter fires, and a background review starts once the reply is out. The fork looks through existing skills, finds nothing to patch in place, and creates pnpm-workspace-test with skill_manage, marked created_by: agent. In a session that supports skill-change notes, the model can learn about it on the next user turn.' },
      { when: 'Session A · turn 40', lane: 'mem', title: 'Context compression triggers a rebuild',
        body: 'invalidate_system_prompt() reloads memory from disk, and the new snapshot says pnpm. A rebuild rewrites the cache anyway, so refreshing memory then costs almost nothing extra (that last part is my inference).' },
      { when: 'Session B · start', lane: 'both', title: 'A new session sees both',
        body: 'MEMORY.md goes into the system prompt; pnpm-workspace-test appears in the skill index, but its body is read only when the model opens it with skill_view.' },
      { when: 'Unused for 30 days', lane: 'skill', title: 'The curator archives it',
        body: 'At the defaults, a maintenance pass can mark it stale after 14 idle days or move it to skills/.archive/ after 30. It can go straight to the archive if the threshold was crossed between checks.' },
      { when: 'The user runs restore', lane: 'skill', title: 'Active again, but the clock is not reset',
        body: 'If nobody reads, uses or patches it before the next curator run, that run archives it again straight away. I confirmed this with an experiment, described below.' },
    ],
  },
};
const t = T[lang] ?? T.zh;
---
<ol class="journey" lang={lang === 'en' ? 'en' : 'zh-CN'}>
  {t.steps.map((s) => (
    <li class={s.lane}>
      <div class="j-when">{s.when}<span class="j-lane">{t.label[s.lane]}</span></div>
      <div class="j-title">{s.title}</div>
      <p class="j-body">{s.body}</p>
    </li>
  ))}
</ol>
<style>
.journey{list-style:none;margin:2em 0;padding:0 0 0 22px;border-left:1px solid var(--line);position:relative}
.journey li{position:relative;padding:0 0 1.5em;margin:0}
.journey li:last-child{padding-bottom:.2em}
.journey li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:-26.5px;top:.55em;width:8px;height:8px;background:var(--bg);border:1.5px solid var(--mute);border-radius:1px}
.journey li.skill::before{border-color:var(--plat)}
.journey li.both::before{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--plat-hi),var(--plat) 55%,var(--plat-lo));border-color:var(--plat)}
.j-when{font:12px/1.6 var(--mono);color:var(--mute);display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.j-lane{color:var(--plat-ink)}
.j-title{font-weight:600;margin:2px 0 4px;line-height:1.6}
.j-body{margin:0!important;color:var(--fg-2);font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.8}
</style>
